      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "2) How is the view API going to scale to support 10s of millions of concurrent requests\nduring popular events?\n\n\nGREAT SOLUTION: Great Solution: Caching, Load Balancing, and Horizontal Scaling\n\n→ Caching\n    → data with high read rates and low update frequency\n        → event details (names, dates, venue information)\n        → performer bio's\n        → location and capacity (static venue details)\n    → { eventId : eventObject } (data shape to be as close as possible to API response}\n    → Read through or cache aside\n    → Cache Invalidation and Consistency\n        → Database triggers to notify caching system of changes (output table/CDC)\n        → TTL policy\n            → Short TTL for frequently updated data\n            → Long TTL for near static data\n\n→ Load Balancing\n    → Use an algo to distribute load across the cluster (round robin, least connections,\nCPU/MEM %)\n\n→ Horizontal Scaling\n    → Event, Search & Booking services are stateless and can be scaled horizontally\nwhen load increases or pre scaled for when we predict high throughput\n\nChallenges\n→ Managing large number of instances and scaling presents operational complexity\n→ Deployments and rollbacks need to be accounted for operational complexity\n→ Generally there can be issues maintining consistency between cache and database,\nthis is not an issue here\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "2) How is the view API going to scale to support 10s of millions of concurrent requests during popular events?\n\n\nGREAT SOLUTION: Great Solution: Caching, Load Balancing, and Horizontal Scaling\n\n→ Caching\n    → data with high read rates and low update frequency\n        → event details (names, dates, venue information)\n        → performer bio's\n        → location and capacity (static venue details)\n    → { eventId : eventObject } (data shape to be as close as possible to API response}\n    → Read through or cache aside\n    → Cache Invalidation and Consistency\n        → Database triggers to notify caching system of changes (output table/CDC)\n        → TTL policy\n            → Short TTL for frequently updated data\n            → Long TTL for near static data\n\n→ Load Balancing\n    → Use an algo to distribute load across the cluster (round robin, least connections, CPU/MEM %)\n\n→ Horizontal Scaling\n    → Event, Search & Booking services are stateless and can be scaled horizontally when load increases or pre scaled for when we predict high throughput\n\nChallenges\n→ Managing large number of instances and scaling presents operational complexity\n→ Deployments and rollbacks need to be accounted for operational complexity\n→ Generally there can be issues maintining consistency between cache and database, this is not an issue here\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
