      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "3) How will the system ensure a good user experience during high-demand events with\nmillions simultaneously booking tickets?\n\n\nGOOD SOLUTION: SSE for Real-Time Seat Updates\n\n→ To ensure seat map is accurate in real time, we can use SSE to push updates\n\nChallenges\n→ For moderatly popular events, this may work\n→ For very popular events, it still presents a bad user experience because seats will fill\nup too fast\n\n\nGREAT SOLUTION: Virtual Waiting Queue for Extremely Popular Events\n\n→ Implement admin enabled, virtual waiting queue system to manage user access\nduring popular events\n→ Flow:\n        → User requests to view booking page, are placed in a virtual queue.\n        → We establish WebSocket connection with client and add the user to the queue\nusing the persistent WebSocket connection\n        → When in front of queue, redirect users via WebSocket connection to book tickets\n        → Simultaneously, update database that user is now allowed to access the booking\nservice\n\nChallenges\n→ Long wait times lead to user frustration, by pushing updates of queue position and\nestimated wait time in real-time, we can lower this risk ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "3) How will the system ensure a good user experience during high-demand events with millions simultaneously booking tickets?\n\n\nGOOD SOLUTION: SSE for Real-Time Seat Updates\n\n→ To ensure seat map is accurate in real time, we can use SSE to push updates\n\nChallenges\n→ For moderatly popular events, this may work\n→ For very popular events, it still presents a bad user experience because seats will fill up too fast\n\n\nGREAT SOLUTION: Virtual Waiting Queue for Extremely Popular Events\n\n→ Implement admin enabled, virtual waiting queue system to manage user access during popular events\n→ Flow:\n        → User requests to view booking page, are placed in a virtual queue.\n        → We establish WebSocket connection with client and add the user to the queue using the persistent WebSocket connection\n        → When in front of queue, redirect users via WebSocket connection to book tickets\n        → Simultaneously, update database that user is now allowed to access the booking service\n\nChallenges\n→ Long wait times lead to user frustration, by pushing updates of queue position and estimated wait time in real-time, we can lower this risk ",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
